    "result": "**Answer:** The electronics dataset is the `g2` group (`items_g2`, plus `fdbk_g2`/`taxn_g2`), identified by product titles (laptop cases, cameras, remotes, speakers, etc.). In `items_g2`, `prc` is a price in cents and `prc_usd` is the same price expressed in dollars (verified: `prc_usd = prc/100` in all 6,570 rows with both values, and no row has one without the other). Averaging the dollar-denominated listed price over the 6,346 electronics products that list a price:\n\n```json\n{\n  \"answer\": 52.96,\n  \"sql\": \"SELECT ROUND(AVG(prc_usd), 2) AS avg_price_usd FROM items_g2\"\n}\n```\n\nThe average listed price of electronics products is **$52.96** (out of 20,000 products, 6,346 have a listed price; NULL prices are excluded from the average).",
